    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) and **Yordan Alvarez** (80.21) anchoring the lineup as our elite offensive pillars. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** earns the top spot on the card against Lorenzen, benefiting from a rare alignment of a favorable park, a 14% platoon edge, and a verified wind blowing out at 5 mph, which pushes his ceiling into the 80s. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in start, utilizing a elite 0.453 xwOBA and a strong SP skill matchup against Melton (xERA 4.61) to maximize our power production. We are also high on **Junior Caminero** (70.04), whose SP skill advantage against Eric Lauer provides the highest margin of safety among our infielders, despite the lingering uncertainty of his lineup placement.\n\nOur bench strategy remains defensive, prioritizing game cap preservation as many of our depth pieces like **Christian Yelich** and **Caleb Durbin** are unavailable today. The closest call for the starting nine was between **Carson Benge** (48.31) and **Dillon Dingler** (42.24); while **Carson Benge** secured the nod due to his premium lead-off spot against Burns, the gap was narrower than expected given the 19% penalty associated with facing an elite arm. We are flagging the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Dillon Dingler**, **Colt Keith**, **Junior Caminero**, and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** as a primary risk factor; should any of these players move down in the order or be rested, the efficiency scores for these slots will drop precipitously, forcing us to lean on the remaining healthy starters to sustain our 5x5 totals. We are closely monitoring **Hyeseong Kim** and **Rece Hinds**, who remain in the minors and are currently not options for us to sub in if these starters are scratched.",
